  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Strong westerly winds on Tuesday could lead to \nsome isolated power outages. Also, the strong wind coupled with \nthe colder temperatures will lead to dangerous wind chills in \nthe mountains Tuesday.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nStrong westerly winds will move in later this afternoon into the\nevening hours. The strongest core of the low-level jet looks to\nmove over nrn areas between 06z and 15z Tuesday. This will bring\ngusts to between 40-50 mph over the higher terrain across the \nnorth, with 65 mph possible at the highest summits. \n\nOver interior Downeast and the Bangor region, expect westerly\nwind gusts between 30 and 40 mph. Existing wind advisory looks\ngood so will leave it as is. It is likely that significant leaf\nloss will occur in areas of Northern Maine where peak foliage \nhas been reached. Additional leaf loss is possible in the \nCentral Highlands to Downeast Maine where the foliage is \nmoderate to high. Gusty winds could also lead to some isolated \npower outages.\n\nWith the colder airmass moving, the strong wind will lead to wind\nchills dangerously cold in the mountains tonight through \nTuesday night. Katahdin will have wind chills in the teens even \nin the middle of the day Tuesday. Hikers should be prepared for \nwinter conditions.",
